# DNA-AND content · how each kind of world's ground, air and clouds are drawn (the terrain kinds)
# radius-km: its size when its system gives none (Earth 6,371 km; Jupiter 69,911; Neptune 24,622; hot Jupiters puffed up
#   to about 1.4 Jupiter widths; the others typical of their kind). solid: has ground (giants have none). water: seas.
# clouds: has a cloud deck; cloud-km: how high it floats; air-km: how deep the air glows at the edge; air-colour: the air's
#   colour at the edge (Rayleigh blue on Earth-like air, dusty orange on deserts, ash-orange over lava). cloud-colour: the
#   clouds' colour (water clouds white; ash grey over lava; ammonia ice cream on gas giants; methane ice pale blue on ice
#   giants; dark haze on hot Jupiters; dust on deserts); cloud-thickness: how much of the sky they cover, 1 full.
# rock-colour: steep bare rock. base-k: its temperature from its star alone, before any greenhouse (Earth 255 K).
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · content/planets.dnat

@terrain default
name: An Earth-like world
radius-km: 6371
solid: yes
water: no
clouds: yes
cloud-km: 9
air-km: 110
air-colour: 0.35 0.56 1
cloud-colour: 0.97 0.97 0.97
cloud-thickness: 1
rock-colour: 0.4 0.38 0.36
base-k: 255

